# How the project gets built, not what ships. Owner's direction — these never reach the
# public repository.
#
# Anchored with a leading slash, and that is not cosmetic. A pattern without one matches a
# directory of that name at ANY depth, so plain `docs/` also swallowed `web/src/app/docs/` —
# the entire documentation section of the site — and `git status` said nothing at all,
# because an ignored file is not an untracked one. Anchoring says what these three always
# meant: the planning folder, the skills folder and the brief, at the root of the repository.
/docs/
/.claude/
/CLAUDE.md

# Rust
cli/target/
**/*.rs.bk

# Angular / Node
web/node_modules/
web/dist/
web/.angular/
web/.nx/
*.tsbuildinfo

# The tool's own working folder, when sloop is run inside this repo during development.
.sloop/

# Secrets and keys — nothing here is ever committed, whatever it is called.
*.age
*.key
*.pem
.secrets/
*.env
!*.env.example

# Backups hold real production data.
backups/

# Editor / OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.log
.idea/
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
